## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Snowflake-core pipeline design: ingestion, streams, tasks, late data handling, and anomaly scoring across accounts.

## Key Concepts
- Snowflake Streams, Tasks, external stages, MERGE, watermarking, rolling baselines, alerting.
- Data governance: access control, masking, retention.

## Code Example
```sql
-- Core objects (illustrative)
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE RAW_EVENTS_STAGE URL='s3://region-lake/raw' FILE_FORMAT=(TYPE='JSON');
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW_EVENTS(
  event_id STRING, customer_id STRING, region STRING, amount NUMBER, ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ
);
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM RAW_EVENTS_STREAM ON TABLE RAW_EVENTS (APPEND_ONLY = FALSE);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_SCORES(customer_id STRING, region STRING, date DATE, score FLOAT);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_WATERMARK(date DATE, max_ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test late-arrival handling and boundary conditions?
- How would you scale the rolling baseline computation to thousands of regions and customers?
